############################
# Strapi
############################

.env
license.txt
exports
.strapi
# The seed is part of the template — a fork's first `pnpm seed:example` has to
# have something to import. Un-ignored narrowly rather than by dropping the
# `data` line: git will not track files under a still-ignored directory, and
# this is also where Strapi drops its exports.
data/*
!data/data.json
!data/flights.example.csv
!data/uploads/
dist
build
.strapi-updater.json
.strapi-cloud.json

# Rewritten from the schemas on every `strapi develop` / `strapi build`, and
# imported by nothing: the UI hand-writes its own model in
# `ui/shared/types/content.ts` (these describe Strapi's internal attribute
# objects, not the JSON the REST API answers with), and `cms/Dockerfile` does
# not copy them. Tracking them only buys a 2,000-line diff every time a
# content type changes.
types/generated/